  "identity": "Leiden University, RIO 50474, ordinary full-time English BSc, September 2026 basis.",
  "curriculum": "The current catalogue tree identifies all year-one and year-two requirements, each totaling 60 EC on exact module entries. In year two, The Politics of Sustainability Solutions replaces Responsible Research and Innovation. Current module entries retain 5 EC for Systems Modelling and 4 EC for Research Design in Practice. Year three catalogue groups identify 30 EC elective space, 18 EC thesis and 12 EC other required work. The current official curriculum chart independently gives 11 EC for Sustainable Societies Project and 1 EC annually for Learning My Way. The field-school listing belongs to the open elective group and does not add required credits.",
  "progression": "Current Science OER pp. 39–41: 45 first-year EC for entry to year two, Mathematics for Sustainability and/or Programming in Python for Systems Modelling, full first year plus 45 year-two EC including Research Design in Practice for the project and thesis, and each preceding Learning My Way unit before the next. The general optional-component rules apply, including Board review when a student proposes mostly first-year units.",
